  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the resilience of the agriculture sector to climate change and strengthening food security in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will establish synergy with the ongoing climate change adaptation projects in the region and leverage UNIDO#s best practices around climate change adaptation in climate vulnerable islands globally. The project interventions will be designed to reinforce the national vision of a prosperous middle-class society in which no one is poor (AmBisyon Natin 2040), the National Agricultural and Fisheries Modernization and Industrialization Plan (2021#2030), the National Adaptation Plan of Action (NAPA), and the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. The project envisioned to build the resilience of small scale farmers, poor households, poor artisanal fishers, and MSMEs by enabling access to postharvest handling technologies, climate resilient technologies, shared agricultural transformation facilities for resilience building, climate finances, accessibility of quality weather information, and promoting economic diversification and generating green jobs for vulnerable youth and women in Mindanao.</narrative>
  </description>
